DESCRIPTION:This listing is for a three session Beginner Knitting Course. 
 The classes will be held in person at Bistitchual on Sunday June 7th\, 14t
 h\, and 21th from 12:30-2:00pm Have you always wanted to learn to knit? We
 ’ve got you covered! Beginner Knitting is a course for brand new beginne
 rs\, and over these three 1.5hr classes\, Mike will teach you everything y
 ou need to create a basic project from beginning to end. Our class size is
  capped at 4 people\, so everyone can receive the attention they need. Mik
 e will share lots of tips and techniques to get you well on your way. (No 
 experience necessary) Materials: Yarn and needles will be provided. What W
 e’ll Learn - How to make a slip knot. - Casting on. - The Knit stitch. -
  The Purl stitch. - Exploring Knit / Purl combinations. - Binding off. - W
 eaving in ends. - Fixing common mistakes and how to avoid them. - Common u
 ses of flat knitting. - Intro into Ravelry. Please note that classes will 
 only proceed if we have a minimum of two attendees . If the minimum is not
  met\, there will be the option for a refund or to reschedule. There will 
 be a four person maximum for each class. Please pre-book your spot to let 
 us know you are coming! About the instructor : Tired of disposing of cloth
 es that were still perfectly wearable\, Mike (he/him) started crafting mai
 nly as a means of mending and repair. This led him to knitting (and later 
 crochet)\, which pretty much immediately became one of his favourite tools
  of self-expression. Cancellation Policy Classes must be paid for at the t
 ime of registration to reserve your spot. - If cancelled 48 hrs or more pr
 ior to the start of the class\, the order will be refunded. Classes cancel
 led less than 48 hrs prior to the start of the class will not be reimburse
 d.
LOCATION:Bistitchual\, 266 Jane St\, Toronto\, ON M6S 3Z2
