DESCRIPTION:This listing is for a two session Beginner Crochet Course. The
  classes will be held in person at Bistitchual on Sunday June 7th and 14th
  from 2:30pm-4:00pm. Learn the fundamentals of crochet in this two part cl
 ass. We will be covering chaining and single crochet\, as well as double a
 nd half-double crochets. Don’t know what any of that means? Great\, you
 ’re in the right place! We’ll provide all the materials\, including a 
 simple pattern that teaches you common terms and instructions you’ll enc
 ounter in most crochet projects. We will also discuss how to choose the ap
 propriate yarn and hook for a project as well as where you can take your c
 rafting after you master these basic techniques. There’s a lot to learn\
 , and we’re excited to accompany your beginning in the wonderful craft o
 f crochet! Materials are included! - 50g ball of worsted weight cotton in 
 your choice of colour - 6mm crochet hook About the instructor: Tired of di
 sposing of clothes that were still perfectly wearable\, Mike (he/him) star
 ted crafting mainly as a means of mending and repair. This led him to knit
 ting (and later crochet)\, which pretty much immediately became one of his
